    {
      "id": "p0133-b003",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Snowdin’s library is denoted by a large sign that says \"LIBRARBY\". This is a simple, childish misspelling of the English word \"library\" that some hasty players might not notice immediately. To achieve the same effect in Japanese, the localizers replaced the misspelled English sign with a similarly misspelled Japanese sign. Instead of としょかん (toshokan, \"library\"), the new sign says としょんか (toshonka), a hilariously bad misspelling that means nothing.",
        "raw": "Snowdin's library is denoted by a large sign that says \"LIBRARBY\". This is\na simple, childish misspelling of the English word \"library\" that some hasty\nplayers might not notice immediately. To achieve the same effect in Japanese,\nthe localizers replaced the misspelled English sign with a similarly misspelled\nJapanese sign. Instead of C. L J: -/plv (toshokan, \"library\"), the new sign says\nC. L J: lvtP (toshonka), a hilariously bad misspelling that means nothing.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en",
          "ja"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.09000845,
          0.23727857,
          0.69111593,
          0.34135
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.0879739,
          0.23656429,
          0.70274338,
          0.34242143
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          13,
          14,
          15,
          16,
          17,
          18
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "Snowdin 图书馆的大招牌写着“LIBRARBY”，把英语 library（图书馆）拼错了。这是个简单、幼稚的拼写错误，匆匆经过的玩家可能一时都注意不到。为了在日语中产生相同效果，本地化人员换上了同样写错的日文招牌：不写“としょかん”（toshokan，图书馆），而写“としょんか”（toshonka），一个毫无意义、错得很好笑的词。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": [
          {
            "start": 120,
            "end": 128,
            "italic": true,
            "lang": "en"
          },
          {
            "start": 144,
