    {
      "id": "p0133-b004",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Originally, the Japanese version of this sign said としよかん (toshiyokan), which isn’t a real word either. The misspelling was less blatant than \"LIBRARBY\" though, so it was changed a few months before Undertale’s Japanese release.",
        "raw": "Originally, the Japanese version of\nthis sign said C. L J: 7'.Plv (toshiyokan),\nwhich isn't a real word either.\nThe misspelling was less blatant\nthan \"LIBRARBY\" though, so it\nwas changed a few months before\nUndertale's Japanese release.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en",
          "ja"
        ],
